# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build context for the backend image (production-deploy checklist §2.7).
#
# Rule: the image must contain the code it runs and nothing else. Every
# excluded path below is either a secret, someone's local state, or material
# that turns a container escape / image pull into a source disclosure.
#
# Verify after building:
#   docker build -f apps/backend/Dockerfile .
#   docker history --no-trunc <image>          # no secrets in any layer
#   find / -name '*.pem' -o -name '.env*'      # inside a running container
#   trivy image --severity HIGH,CRITICAL <image>
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Version control: the whole history is a source disclosure and often
# contains secrets that were deleted from the working tree (§1.2).
.git
.gitignore
.githooks

# Secrets and local environment (§1.3.1). The image mounts the payer keypair
# at run time; it must never be baked into a layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
**/keys
**/keys/**
**/*-keypair.json
**/id.json
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.keystore
**/secrets
**/secrets/**
**/serviceAccount*.json

# Dependencies and build output: reinstalled inside the image from the
# lockfile, and dist/ is produced by the build stage.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/target
**/build
.anchor
test-ledger

# Tests, fixtures and tooling that do not run in production.
**/tests
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.mjs
**/*.test.js
**/coverage
security-reports
**/db-bench.json

# Documentation and repositories of internal notes: not needed at runtime and
# a rich source of accidental disclosure (§2.5).
docs
**/docs
*.md
!README.md
**/*.example.env

# Local tooling state.
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/.vscode
**/.idea
.python-version
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
scripts/devnet-legacy
apps/web
